{
  "_README": [
    "A/B variant definitions for the Kalshi weather paper trader.",
    "Each arm is a parallel paper book: its own state/<dir>/ trading the SAME live",
    "order books with a different env/argv config. bin/run_variants.py loops these;",
    "bin/compare_variants.py + bin/premium_fill_report.py report across them.",
    "",
    "FOCUS (2026-06-21): the only edge is premium capture; the open problem is",
    "EXECUTION/FILLS. Most arms below A/B the premium quote placement + fill model.",
    "",
    "Per-arm fields:",
    "  name        identifier (used in the reports)",
    "  enabled     run this arm in the cycle?",
    "  live        REAL orders. Only runs when env LIVE=1; runner syncs the live book",
    "              first (sync_live_positions.py) and passes --live. Money at risk.",
    "  dir         state subdir under state/ (paper-book/log location)",
    "  fv          fair-values file (relative to repo root); falls back to fair-values.json",
    "  mode        paper_trade.py --mode: 'mm' (post makers) or 'taker' (hit ask)",
    "  max_orders  paper_trade.py --max-orders",
    "  postmortem  drain loss queue into GLOBAL LESSONS.md? Keep true only for 'main'.",
    "  dashboard   write dashboard/data.json? Keep true only for 'main' (single fixed path).",
    "  env         KALSHI_WEATHER_* overrides for this arm.",
    "",
    "Premium execution knobs: PREMIUM_QUOTE_OFFSET (0=join bid, +n=inside spread,",
    "-n=passive), ADVERSE_MARGIN_CENTS + FILL_DEPTH_FRAC (fill-model realism),",
    "PREMIUM_MAX_SPREAD + PREMIUM_MIN/MAX_CENTS (band/spread tightness)."
  ],
  "variants": [
    {
      "name": "main",
      "enabled": true,
      "dir": "paper",
